So now we're going to visit 
organization and communities

00:14:48.320 --> 00:14:51.557
further west. Starting in the
Windy City Chicago, Illinois.

00:14:51.657 --> 00:14:55.527
Where there's an increase of 
HIV AIDS related cases

00:14:55.527 --> 00:14:57.663
among African-American
men.

00:15:01.566 --> 00:15:05.136
At the close of 2015,
more than 24,000 people

00:15:05.136 --> 00:15:07.673
were living with HIV in
Chicago, Illinois.

00:15:07.673 --> 00:15:11.510
Proactive a local nonprofit
organization

00:15:11.510 --> 00:15:14.846
is on the front lines. Training
and equipping community health

00:15:14.980 --> 00:15:17.715
workers on how to deal with 
the HIV epidemic.

00:15:17.749 --> 00:15:20.018
There are actually four 
institutions involved.

00:15:20.152 --> 00:15:21.853
Two community based
institutions

00:15:21.987 --> 00:15:24.489
and two academic
institutions.

00:15:24.489 --> 00:15:29.828
One is South Suburban 
College and that's out here

00:15:29.828 --> 00:15:31.997
and that's a two year
instituiton.

00:15:31.997 --> 00:15:35.500
The other is Chicago 
State University.

00:15:35.500 --> 00:15:38.103
These Step Up students 
will eventually become

00:15:38.203 --> 00:15:40.338
community health workers 
helping residents by

00:15:40.438 --> 00:15:44.209
educating them on HIV
prevention and treatment methods

00:15:44.209 --> 00:15:46.178
through the use of tablets.

00:15:46.178 --> 00:15:48.513
I know that in the future with
the career choice

00:15:48.513 --> 00:15:50.849
that I've chosen this is going
to be a great tool for me

00:15:50.849 --> 00:15:55.587
because information that I share
will be from a reliable source.

00:15:55.587 --> 00:15:59.891
Proactive will train 93 Step Up
students on NLM resources.

00:15:59.891 --> 00:16:02.694
This will be part of an
interactive digital lesson plan

00:16:02.694 --> 00:16:05.430
and Proactive's interactive 
healthcare readiness program.

00:16:05.430 --> 00:16:07.532
I thought that I had the
resources that I needed

00:16:07.632 --> 00:16:10.201
to talk about HIV

00:16:10.268 --> 00:16:13.138
but as I began to go on 
this particular website

00:16:13.138 --> 00:16:17.141
I learned more and more
and it was more truthful

00:16:17.141 --> 00:16:18.410
and accurate information.

00:16:18.477 --> 00:16:20.712
The tablets community health
workers learn to navigate

00:16:20.745 --> 00:16:24.783
NLM resources on will prove
useful at off site partner

00:16:24.783 --> 00:16:26.251
organizations.

00:16:26.251 --> 00:16:29.254
Allowing them the opportunity 
to meet people where they are

00:16:29.388 --> 00:16:31.789
with vital and accurate HIV 
prevention and treatment

00:16:31.890 --> 00:16:33.892
information.

00:16:33.892 --> 00:16:36.795
We have high risk populations
so they are hard to find and

00:16:36.828 --> 00:16:39.064
hard to locate.

00:16:39.064 --> 00:16:42.401
But our team has really
been able to go in there

00:16:42.401 --> 00:16:46.905
and do segmented outreach
and locate those individuals

00:16:46.972 --> 00:16:49.274
that are positive.

00:16:49.274 --> 00:16:52.444
Increasing numbers of 
qualified health care workers

00:16:52.444 --> 00:16:55.748
to meet the increasing need
to treat HIV patients.

00:17:06.258 --> 00:17:08.526
On any given day one to
two hundred people

00:17:08.526 --> 00:17:10.662
pass through the Mexican
Consulate

00:17:10.762 --> 00:17:12.764
in Salt Lake City, Utah.

00:17:12.764 --> 00:17:16.334
And a good portion of those 
people are just waiting.

00:17:16.334 --> 00:17:19.371
And there's absolutely nothing 
there to do they just sit there

00:17:19.371 --> 00:17:21.173
and stare at the wall 
pretty much.

00:17:21.173 --> 00:17:23.642
So we use that time 
with a "promotora"

00:17:23.675 --> 00:17:24.776
our community health worker.

00:17:24.810 --> 00:17:27.012
And they take full advantage 
of it.

00:17:27.012 --> 00:17:29.714
Transforming waiting time 
into a meaningful

00:17:29.714 --> 00:17:31.482
health learning experience.

00:17:31.482 --> 00:17:34.719
The biggest way that HIV has
effected our community members

00:17:34.819 --> 00:17:37.623
is the fact that it's not
something that we talk about

00:17:37.656 --> 00:17:41.459
and it's not something that
we necessarily know about.

00:17:41.493 --> 00:17:44.629
Getting pertinent health
information from a familiar face

00:17:44.629 --> 00:17:47.632
also makes a big impact on
those served.

00:17:47.632 --> 00:17:49.334
[speaking in Spanish]

00:18:09.321 --> 00:18:11.656
Information they may have never
come across

00:18:11.689 --> 00:18:14.659
due to the language barriers 
they face in the US

00:18:14.659 --> 00:18:16.862
and the cultural barriers 
they face back home.

00:18:16.862 --> 00:18:19.498
We invite them into the
Ventanilla de Salud

00:18:19.498 --> 00:18:20.766
to get tested.

00:18:20.766 --> 00:18:24.602
We do blood pressure, glucose 
and BMI testing and at the end

00:18:24.736 --> 00:18:27.439
of every person coming in 
to getting the testing

00:18:27.439 --> 00:18:31.276
we do a one-on-one session
to go over the websites again

00:18:31.276 --> 00:18:33.745
to reinforce that these websites
are available to them

00:18:33.745 --> 00:18:37.916
to get HIV AIDS info but also
other health related information

00:18:37.916 --> 00:18:39.951
Ciriac Alvares

00:18:39.951 --> 00:18:42.788
They've connected over 300
people to health resources

00:18:42.788 --> 00:18:44.956
with the help of the
National Library of Medicine

00:18:45.090 --> 00:18:47.091
including Ciriac Alvarez.

00:18:47.091 --> 00:18:49.560
There is one website in 
particular

00:18:49.560 --> 00:18:51.229
that Alejandra showed me 
where you can find

00:18:51.229 --> 00:18:54.699
like HIV testing places by like
putting in your zip code

00:18:54.799 --> 00:18:55.967
and it's really cool.

00:18:55.967 --> 00:18:59.805
From those surveys we've been
able to realize that

00:18:59.905 --> 00:19:03.541
the work that our "promotoras"
are doing is valuable and it

00:19:03.541 --> 00:19:06.478
works because we see an increase
of knowledge from the before

00:19:06.478 --> 00:19:10.115
and after of our community
members when they receive the

00:19:10.115 --> 00:19:12.317
workshop and are able to
access their resources.

00:19:12.317 --> 00:19:15.253
Assisting yet another person
to their right to

00:19:15.253 --> 00:19:18.923
life, liberty, and the pursuit
of healthiness.

00:19:18.923 --> 00:19:19.423
life, liberty, and the pursuit
of healthine[music]

00:19:36.341 --> 00:19:39.243
Time Magazine dubbed
the year 2014 the

00:19:39.243 --> 00:19:41.279
Transgender Tipping
Point.

00:19:41.279 --> 00:19:43.348
From the red carpet and
the runway

00:19:43.348 --> 00:19:47.151
to politics and entertainment, 
transgender people

00:19:47.151 --> 00:19:48.853
truly were everywhere.

00:19:48.853 --> 00:19:51.156
But for many transgender
youth

00:19:51.156 --> 00:19:54.526
the notoriety has not created
impactful change in their

00:19:54.526 --> 00:19:55.527
daily lives.

00:19:55.527 --> 00:19:57.195
Nowhere is that more
apparent

00:19:57.195 --> 00:19:59.364
than in the area of
healthcare.

00:19:59.364 --> 00:20:02.867
Transgender youth they have
challenges

00:20:02.867 --> 00:20:04.703
they have requirements

00:20:04.703 --> 00:20:06.370
and they don't know where
to go to get

00:20:06.370 --> 00:20:07.506
their questions answered.

00:20:07.539 --> 00:20:09.274
They don't know where to go
to get services

00:20:09.274 --> 00:20:10.776
that are youth friendly.

00:20:10.776 --> 00:20:14.045
With provider's that understand 
the needs that are quite unique

00:20:14.045 --> 00:20:15.213
for the Transgender community.

00:20:15.213 --> 00:20:17.382
Headquartered in the Bay Area
of California.

00:20:17.382 --> 00:20:19.984
The mecca of LGBTQ rights.

00:20:19.984 --> 00:20:24.188
YTH is the partner of choice 
for those in search of new ways

00:20:24.188 --> 00:20:26.992
to advance health of youth
and young adults

00:20:26.992 --> 00:20:27.992
through technology.

00:20:27.992 --> 00:20:29.861
In addition to those health
disparities

00:20:29.861 --> 00:20:32.564
youth are also kind of
faced with they're dependent

00:20:32.564 --> 00:20:33.331
on their parents.

00:20:33.465 --> 00:20:35.066
They don't necessarily have
an income.

00:20:35.066 --> 00:20:36.901
So if they come out to their
parents

00:20:36.901 --> 00:20:38.403
and they're not receiving 
support

00:20:38.403 --> 00:20:40.472
I mean where do you go 
from there?

00:20:40.572 --> 00:20:43.074
And that is why they
developed they2ze.

00:20:43.074 --> 00:20:46.244
A mobile app that brings 
together all the Bay Area

00:20:46.244 --> 00:20:48.547
resources for transgender
spectrum youth.

00:20:48.547 --> 00:20:53.084
So the design itself was really
guided by our brainstorming

00:20:53.084 --> 00:20:56.754
process and meeting with the
transgender youth community

00:20:56.754 --> 00:20:58.356
and our advisory board.

00:20:58.356 --> 00:21:00.591
So that sort of kicked off the
design process where we got

00:21:00.591 --> 00:21:04.095
feedback from them on what they 
would like to see in the app.

00:21:04.095 --> 00:21:05.930
When somebody uses the app and 
they are searching

00:21:05.930 --> 00:21:10.602
for a certain answer
a certain search term

00:21:10.602 --> 00:21:13.104
a lot of the resources that end
up coming up

00:21:13.104 --> 00:21:14.906
are actually NLM resources.

00:21:14.906 --> 00:21:17.909
The app is available in the 
Apple or Android app store

00:21:18.009 --> 00:21:21.079
and has features that allow 
you to find community hangouts

00:21:21.079 --> 00:21:24.783
testing sites and doctors
like Doctor Scott Mosser

00:21:24.783 --> 00:21:28.386
a internationally renowned
board-certifed plastic surgeon

00:21:28.386 --> 00:21:30.088
based in San Francisco.

00:21:30.088 --> 00:21:34.626
I think the app is expansive
for trans healthcare resources.

00:21:34.626 --> 00:21:38.096
So any individual that's 
looking for an HIV doctor

00:21:38.196 --> 00:21:41.233
again blood pressure doctor
or a diabetes doctor

00:21:41.299 --> 00:21:44.102
for any reason but wants to
make sure that they're

00:21:44.102 --> 00:21:47.372
gender inclusive and
understanding of their

00:21:47.372 --> 00:21:49.640
potential gender needs
as well

00:21:49.640 --> 00:21:52.110
those are the individuals all
who would be using the app.

00:21:52.110 --> 00:21:54.712
Giving Bay Area transgender 
youth

00:21:54.712 --> 00:21:56.948
their moment for a
better life.

00:22:09.794 --> 00:22:11.963
You have just seen the 
technical processes

00:22:11.963 --> 00:22:17.468
each ACIOP awardee took to 
disseminate NLM HIV information.

00:22:17.468 --> 00:22:19.837
D'Vinci upgraded a conventional 
print magazine

00:22:19.937 --> 00:22:22.140
with a scenario based e-learning
module

00:22:22.140 --> 00:22:24.809
interwoven with resources 
from NLM.

00:22:24.809 --> 00:22:27.779
El Centro used interactive
graphic novels

00:22:27.779 --> 00:22:30.648
to disseminate NLM information.

00:22:30.681 --> 00:22:34.518
Black Girl Health used an 
influential social media

00:22:34.518 --> 00:22:36.188
celebrity to bring minority
women together

00:22:36.288 --> 00:22:38.757
to learn about NLM 
information resources.

00:22:38.857 --> 00:22:41.259
Norfolk State University
developed iBooks

00:22:41.359 --> 00:22:45.864
that combined dramatic
arts with NLM information

00:22:45.864 --> 00:22:47.332
to engage youth.

00:22:47.332 --> 00:22:50.868
Proactive Community Services
engaged students

00:22:50.868 --> 00:22:52.370
pursuing health careers

00:22:52.370 --> 00:22:54.372
to use tablets to become
proficient

00:22:54.372 --> 00:22:55.940
with NLM resources.

00:22:55.940 --> 00:22:59.277
Communities United used
the Mexican Consulate

00:22:59.277 --> 00:23:01.012
as a technology center 
to educate

00:23:01.012 --> 00:23:04.216
Spanish speaking immigrants
on NLM resources

00:23:04.216 --> 00:23:05.783
and HIV information.

00:23:05.783 --> 00:23:09.888
And lastly YTH served 
transgender youth

00:23:09.888 --> 00:23:12.557
by developing a mobile 
phone app

00:23:12.557 --> 00:23:15.693
using NLM information 
to meet the special needs

00:23:15.693 --> 00:23:17.561
of this population

00:23:17.561 --> 00:23:19.831
After showing all the
technical approaches

00:23:19.831 --> 00:23:22.367
used to disseminate
NLM resources

00:23:22.367 --> 00:23:24.135
we hope you see the 
awardees

00:23:24.135 --> 00:23:27.038
as key stakeholders 
that aligned their efforts

00:23:27.038 --> 00:23:29.206
to address an ongoing 
health crisis.

00:23:29.206 --> 00:23:31.676
In addition the National 
Library of Medicine

00:23:31.676 --> 00:23:34.812
as an emerging leader in
innovative approaches

00:23:34.812 --> 00:23:37.315
to raising awareness
around HIV and AIDS.

00:23:37.315 --> 00:23:39.651
We'd like to thank NLM
for promoting

00:23:39.651 --> 00:23:41.853
cutting edge technology 
to support

00:23:41.853 --> 00:23:44.856
HIV and AIDS prevention 
and treatment information.

00:23:44.989 --> 00:23:47.258
As well as supporting each
awardees

00:23:47.258 --> 00:23:50.729
creative uses of
NLM's resources.

